sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-02--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch11-02: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.35";
    dc:description "That a fixed external direction cannot wind a growing structure into a spiral is a kinematic argument, not a dataset result. The biological claim that the co-rotating force is the columellar muscle needs measurements that have not been archived. Shell collections can show that spirals exist and cannot show which force produced them or exclude other intrinsic growth asymmetries.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The empirical residue is whether a force that turns with the growing body, identified with the columellar muscle in snails, is what produces the spiral, as opposed to an external field of constant direction. That requires force or muscle-activity measurements during growth, not shell outline alone.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "No public dataset records muscle force through shell coiling.", "Shell shape is compatible with any intrinsic asymmetry of growth and does not identify the columellar muscle as the deflecting force.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.57"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.35"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch11-02--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of thompson1917-ch11-02 by Grok 4.7: 0.3";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
